# Per-Dockerfile ignore file (BuildKit). Applies ONLY to builds that use the sibling
# source/<Service>/Dockerfile, and takes precedence over the root .dockerignore.
#
# Why this exists instead of a plain .dockerignore in this directory:
# the build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, not source/. AuthAPI, UserAPI and
# NotificationAPI reference ../../contracts/auth/auth.csproj, which lives outside
# source/, and Docker cannot COPY from outside the build context — so the context has
# to contain both source/ and contracts/.
#
# The root .dockerignore excludes source/ (correct for the ai-service build) and must
# stay exactly as it is. This file overrides it for .NET image builds only.
# See docs/architecture/phase1-checklist.md, Batch A and blocker B-1.

# --- Version control and tooling metadata (.git alone is ~552 MB) ---
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.agents/
.tmp/

# --- Other build contexts and large trees no .NET image needs ---
ai-service/
infra/
docs/

# --- Build output and IDE state ---
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/node_modules/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# --- Secrets: injected as environment variables at runtime, never baked into a layer ---
.env
.env.example
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/secrets.json

# --- Documentation ---
**/*.md

# --- Local-only artifacts. Untracked on the current machine, but excluded so they
#     can never enter the build context on any clone. Added during implementation,
#     beyond the literal Batch A spec — see the Batch A handover note. ---
*.docx
Sequence and class/
bin_verify/
